  "question": {
    "text": "A metal wire of uniform mass density having length $L$ and mass $M$ is bent to form a semicircular arc and a particle of mass $\\mathrm{m}$ is placed at the centre of the arc. The gravitational force on the particle by the wire is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{GmM} \\pi^2}{\\mathrm{~L}^2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{GMm} \\pi}{2 \\mathrm{~L}^2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$0$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\frac{2 \\mathrm{GmM} \\pi}{\\mathrm{L}^2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0024_88ea77d72086.png\"><br />We have $R=\\frac{L}{\\pi}$\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& \\mathrm{g}_0=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{G} \\frac{\\mathrm{M}}{\\mathrm{L}}}{\\mathrm{R}}=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{GM} \\pi}{\\mathrm{L}^2} \\\\\n& \\therefore \\mathrm{F}_{\\mathrm{m}}=\\mathrm{mg}_0=\\frac{2 \\mathrm{GM} \\pi \\mathrm{m}}{\\mathrm{L}^2}\n\\end{aligned}$<br />Hence option (4)"
  }
}